.nh
.TH "PB-DOMAIN-SHOW" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-domain-show - Show a domain's DNS records, status and uses


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb domain show <domain> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Show one domain: its DNS records, verification state, certificate state and expiry, the fix
for a failed check, and the tunnels and previews that use it. Name it by hostname or ID; case
and a trailing dot are ignored.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for show

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb domain show dev.example.com
  pb domain show dev.example.com --json
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-domain(1)\fP
